		<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
		<personalityDescription>Trusting Albiona is a mistake most people only make once. She weaves a careful web of half-truths and false assurances, making it nearly impossible to tell where her real motives lie - until she&apos;s already gotten what she wanted. Albiona used to trust mission briefings - until she saw too many bad calls end in disaster. Now, she refuses to blindly follow anything. If a plan isn&apos;t bulletproof, she&apos;s going to tear it apart - because in war, the ones who don&apos;t question bad plans end up dead. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Smiles like a friend, schemes like an enemy. Don&apos;t turn your back.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
