		<personalityDescription>Teague says what he means and means what he says. He doesn&apos;t believe in playing games or sugarcoating the truth - his words and actions come from a place of honesty, making him a rare presence in a world full of deception. Before every battle, Teague follows the same sequence: adjusts his gloves twice, tightens his straps in the same order, taps his helmet once. &quot;Superstition?&quot; someone asks. &quot;No,&quot; he replies. &quot;Just making sure everything&apos;s right.&quot; But his squad knows - if his routine is ever disrupted, he&apos;s off his game. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 36%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Speaks plain. Earns trust the old-fashioned way.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
