		<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
		<personalityDescription>Afzal didn&apos;t get this far by being naive. He&apos;s seen every trick, survived every scam, and learned how to play the game better than most. He trusts no one, always keeps an edge, and makes sure he&apos;s the one doing the exploiting - not the other way around. Afzal is always moving - tapping his fingers on his leg, adjusting his gloves, shifting his stance even when in cover. His squad used to think he was anxious, but no - this is just how he operates. He says he fights better when he&apos;s in motion. And judging by his reaction time, he might actually be right. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Not fooled easily. Seen the worst, and learned to profit from it.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
