		<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
		<personalityDescription>Jason is convinced he&apos;s the best warrior, the best tactician, and probably the smartest person in the room. He doesn&apos;t just believe in himself - he assumes everyone else is playing catch-up, whether they realize it or not. Jason puts on a friendly face, but it&apos;s a survival tactic as much as anything. He knows being likable keeps people from turning on him, but deep down, he&apos;s always waiting for the moment when trust becomes a liability. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Assumes superiority in everything. Believes others are just trying to catch up.&lt;br&gt;- Knows every name, every story. Makes people feel like they matter.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
