		<personalityDescription>Indecision is just another form of weakness, and Ambroz refuses to entertain it. He makes the call, moves forward, and never looks back - because in the brutal reality of war, second-guessing gets people killed. Ambroz doesn&apos;t just like to lead - he needs to. Every decision, every plan, every battle has to go his way, and he expects absolute obedience. Anything less is just another problem to be dealt with. </personalityDescription>
