		<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
		<personalityDescription>Julius does what&apos;s required, nothing more, nothing less. He isn&apos;t lazy - he just sees ambition as a fool&apos;s game, one that leads to stress, betrayal, and an early grave. Julius is convinced he can handle anything, no matter how big the challenge. He stretches himself thin, takes on risks he shouldn&apos;t, and charges ahead without thinking about whether he can actually pull it off - because failure isn&apos;t part of his vocabulary. Yet. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 62%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Not lazy, just finished trying. No threat, no spark.&lt;br&gt;- Thinks confidence replaces planning. Runs headfirst into collapse.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
