		<personalityDescription>Anabell puts in the work, no matter how long it takes. Whether it&apos;s maintaining her combat unit, planning battle strategies, or honing her skills, she refuses to cut corners - because in her mind, effort is what separates the competent from the dead. Anabell doesn&apos;t just enjoy the rush - she needs it. In the quiet moments, her hands shake, her mind won&apos;t stop racing. But when the crisis hits? She&apos;s steady, clear, unbreakable. Because if she&apos;s not in danger, she&apos;s not sure who she even is anymore. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Puts in the hours. Refuses shortcuts - effort equals survival.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
