		<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
		<personalityDescription>Fath doesn&apos;t need brute force when a few well-placed words can do the job. He weaves half-truths and clever deceptions with ease, turning enemies against each other while he walks away unscathed - and usually richer. Win or lose, Fath follows the exact same steps after every engagement. He cleans his weapon the same way, checks his gear in the same order, and takes a deep breath at the same moment in the process. &quot;It&apos;s about discipline,&quot; he insists. His squad suspects it&apos;s about something else entirely. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Words over weapons. Turns enemies on each other, walks off clean.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
