		<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
		<personalityDescription>Patience has never been Clint&apos;s strong suit. He leans forward in every briefing, itching to get moving, his restless energy practically vibrating through the room. Sitting still isn&apos;t an option - he lives for action, for motion, for doing something. Clint has seen how large-scale strategies sacrifice the people actually fighting. He&apos;s seen plans drawn up by those who never have to bleed for them. He trusts what&apos;s real, what he can see, what he can control. Because he knows that when things go wrong, it&apos;s not the planners who suffer - it&apos;s the ones actually in the fight. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Can&apos;t sit still - lives for the green light.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
