		<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
		<personalityDescription>Ferit gives because he knows what it&apos;s like to have nothing. He&apos;ll take the hard jobs, give up his share, and put himself in danger for the sake of others - even when it costs him more than he can afford to lose. Ferit pranks because if he stops, he&apos;ll have to process the horror around him. Every practical joke is a distraction, a way to keep things light even when the air feels like death. The day Ferit stops joking is the day his squad knows things have truly gone to hell. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Gives more than they should. Probably won&apos;t stop until it breaks them.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
