		<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
		<personalityDescription>Planning has never been Daniel&apos;s strong suit. He follows instinct over strategy, letting adrenaline and quick thinking dictate his path. Sometimes it works, sometimes it doesn&apos;t - but either way, he never hesitates. No matter how bleak things get, Daniel refuses to let doubt take hold. He reminds his unit why they fight, why they push forward, and why they can&apos;t afford to give up - because in his mind, defeat is only a state of mind. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Strategy ignored. Runs on instinct and adrenaline. Sometimes lucky, always fast.&lt;br&gt;- Refuses to let despair settle in. Might be the reason the line holds.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
