		<personalityDescription>Sadao could probably win more fights if they didn&apos;t spend so much time starting them. Whether it&apos;s trash-talking over comms or throwing the first punch in a negotiation, they seem to believe the best way to solve a problem is by making it someone else&apos;s problem. Fist first. No matter what gets thrown at them, Sadao bounces back. Whether it&apos;s a brutal loss, a catastrophic failure, or a battlefield injury, they refuse to let anything break them. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Starts problems just to end them violently. First to swing, last to think.&lt;br&gt;- Takes the hit, gets back up. Nothing breaks them for long.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
