		<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
		<personalityDescription>To Jeroen, hesitation is just another word for failure. They throw caution aside, charging headlong into danger with raw aggression and an utter disregard for self-preservation. If survival means second-guessing, then maybe survival isn&apos;t worth it. Jeroen doesn&apos;t see the point in chasing titles or prestige. As long as they&apos;re comfortable and things run smoothly, they have no interest in making life harder for themself just to impress others. </personalityDescription>
		<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Ignores self-preservation. Sees hesitation as death. Risk of early burnout.&lt;br&gt;- Happy to coast. Won&apos;t break things - won&apos;t fix them either.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
